<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Splunk EVPN Assurance — Verification Report</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
         margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 60rem; color: #1b1b1b; }
  h1 { color: #049fd9; border-bottom: 2px solid #049fd9; padding-bottom: .3rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #d6d6d6; padding: .5rem .7rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #f2f7fa; }
  code { background: #f4f4f4; padding: .1rem .3rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  pre { background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: 4px; }
  .pass { color: #0b7a3e; font-weight: 600; }
  .fail { color: #c3262e; font-weight: 600; }
  .score { font-size: 1.2rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Splunk EVPN Assurance — Verification Report</h1>

<p>
  <strong>Site:</strong> {{ assurance_site }}<br>
  <strong>Splunk host:</strong> {{ ansible_host }}<br>
  <strong>Index:</strong> <code>{{ splunk_assurance_index }}</code><br>
  <strong>Generated:</strong> {{ ansible_date_time.iso8601 | default(lookup('pipe', 'date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')) }}
</p>

<p class="score">
  <span class="{{ 'pass' if (_assurance_rows | rejectattr('ok') | list | length == 0) else 'fail' }}">
    {{ _assurance_rows | selectattr('ok') | list | length }} / {{ _assurance_rows | length }} checks passed
  </span>
</p>

<table>
  <tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Observed</th><th>Result</th></tr>
{% for row in _assurance_rows %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ row.label }}</td>
    <td><code>{{ row.expected }}</code></td>
    <td><code>{{ row.observed }}</code></td>
    <td class="{{ 'pass' if row.ok else 'fail' }}">{{ 'PASS' if row.ok else 'FAIL' }}</td>
  </tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>Pipeline under test</h2>
<pre>
{{ assurance_site }} fabric  --MDT gRPC--&gt;  {{ ansible_host }}:{{ otel_receiver_port }}
                                              |
                                      splunk_hec exporter
                                              v
                                   {{ splunk_hec_url }}
                                              |
                                              v
                                index={{ splunk_assurance_index }} (metric)
                                              |
                                              v
                                   app: {{ splunk_app_name }}
</pre>

<h2>Reading a failure</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Failing check</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Collector service running</td>
      <td><code>{{ otel_service_name }}</code> is down. <code>journalctl -u {{ otel_service_name }} -n 50</code>.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Fabric devices streaming</td>
      <td>Subscriptions are not dialling out. Check <code>show telemetry ietf subscription all receivers</code> on a switch, and that <code>telemetry.splunk.receiver_ip</code> in <code>settings.json</code> matches {{ ansible_host }}.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>HEC export failures</td>
      <td>The collector reaches the fabric but cannot write to Splunk. Check the HEC token and that <code>{{ splunk_assurance_index }}</code> is a <strong>metric</strong> index.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Nodes resolving through the lookup</td>
      <td>Metrics are arriving but <code>cisco.node_id</code> does not match the <code>hostname</code> column of <code>evpn_device_inventory.csv</code>. Re-run stage 05, then compare a raw <code>| mstats ... BY "cisco.node_id"</code> against the CSV.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Dashboard Studio validation</td>
      <td>A panel query or view definition is broken. Run <code>tools/validate_studio.py</code> directly for the per-panel detail.</td></tr>
</table>

</body>
</html>
